Subject: [PATCH] transport: accommodate full-roster AP metrics reports

The fixed 100-client lab can concentrate most stations on one agent. Its
monitor reports fit individually, but aggregating traffic, link, extended link
and Wi-Fi 6 status TLVs exceeds the 8 KiB agent buffer. Allocation fails before
send, so the controller receives no station measurements from that agent.
Concentration on a single radio can also exceed the monitor's old buffer.

Raise the bounded application and broker frame capacities together to 32 KiB.
This retains one complete response with its original MID and all station TLVs;
the existing transport fragments at TLV boundaries for Ethernet. The limit
remains below the 64 KiB reassembly budget and 16-bit CMDU length field. No
reporting frequency, measurement, policy or wire format changes. Rebuild and
deploy every mesh node, including its transport process, as one artifact.

The lab's native broker observer must accept the same bounded frame size.
The capacity regression serializes and parses 100 stations with their traffic,
link, extended-link and eight-TID status TLVs using production TLVF classes.
Run tests/test_native_metrics_capacity.py with PRPL_NATIVE_INSTALL pointing to
the built native install. Its original 8 KiB negative control must fail; 100
stations across 1, 9 and 15 BSSes require 10,299-10,985 bytes and must round-trip
without losing MID, counters, RCPI or any TID entries. The passive decoder tests
separately cover split stream delivery above 8 KiB and oversized rejection.
Live qualification still requires full-roster fresh metrics, native counter
trials and the existing memory gate; serialization alone is not sufficient.

